1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:03,294
<i>The last time we ate at a place like this</i>

2
00:00:03,378 --> 00:00:05,422
<i>was when your sister Abi got promoted.</i>

3
00:00:05,505 --> 00:00:08,341
<i>And now, it's you.</i>

4
00:00:08,425 --> 00:00:11,886
<i>That's why I told you</i>
<i>to just trust me, Ma.</i>

5
00:00:12,512 --> 00:00:15,515
<i>It was Benilda Cariño herself</i>
<i>who invited me out for dinner.</i>

6
00:00:15,598 --> 00:00:17,392
<i>I should be the one handling this, Ma.</i>

7
00:00:17,475 --> 00:00:20,603
<i>Let me be the judge</i>
<i>if you made the right choice</i>

8
00:00:20,687 --> 00:00:22,605
<i>in investing in this shady company.</i>

9
00:00:22,689 --> 00:00:25,358
<i>I have a reservation under Billy Cariño.</i>

10
00:00:25,442 --> 00:00:27,861
[MARIELA] <i>Are you following my daughter?!</i>

11
00:00:29,863 --> 00:00:31,072
<i>Cat got your tongue?</i>

12
00:00:31,156 --> 00:00:32,699
<i>Excuse me.</i>

13
00:00:34,617 --> 00:00:35,910
<i>How dare you?!</i>

14
00:00:37,829 --> 00:00:39,414
<i>Let go of my mother.</i>

15
00:00:39,497 --> 00:00:41,041
<i>- Ma.</i>
<i>- Karma will get you one day!</i>

16
00:00:41,124 --> 00:00:42,292
<i>I'll be waiting.</i>

17
00:00:46,671 --> 00:00:49,466
[Rowena] <i>I know you're doing this</i>
<i>because Charm is your friend.</i>

18
00:00:49,549 --> 00:00:53,052
<i>And while I admire you</i>
<i>for being a good friend,</i>

19
00:00:53,636 --> 00:00:55,638
<i>I also need to be a good mother.</i>

20
00:00:56,389 --> 00:00:59,017
<i>- Billy. Billy, I'm sorry.</i>
<i>- It's okay.</i>

21
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:00,435
<i>It's not okay, Ralph.</i>

22
00:01:00,518 --> 00:01:02,187
<i>We're going to pull out.</i>

23
00:01:02,270 --> 00:01:04,064
<i>This company is not good for you,</i>

24
00:01:04,147 --> 00:01:06,066
<i>especially that girlfriend of yours!</i>

25
00:01:06,149 --> 00:01:07,233
<i>Excuse me, ma'am.</i>

26
00:01:07,317 --> 00:01:09,861
<i>But have you tried</i>
<i>getting to know Charm personally?</i>

27
00:01:09,944 --> 00:01:12,322
<i>I hope you'll also give her a chance.</i>

28
00:01:12,405 --> 00:01:14,157
[ROWENA] <i>This meeting</i>

29
00:01:14,240 --> 00:01:15,450
<i>is done.</i>

30
00:01:15,533 --> 00:01:16,743
[RALPH] <i>You don't know my mom.</i>

31
00:01:17,410 --> 00:01:20,538
<i>She'll do anything to get her way.</i>

32
00:01:20,622 --> 00:01:23,666
<i>But now, it's time for me</i>
<i>to be a better boyfriend.</i>

33
00:01:23,750 --> 00:01:25,335
<i>I need to make a stand.</i>

34
00:01:25,418 --> 00:01:27,837
<i>I don't care if she gets mad.</i>

35
00:01:27,921 --> 00:01:29,214
[JORDAN]<i> See?</i>

36
00:01:29,297 --> 00:01:30,673
<i>That's your magic.</i>

37
00:01:31,341 --> 00:01:32,550
<i>You're like Cupid.</i>

38
00:01:32,634 --> 00:01:35,386
<i>- That's why you're perfect for LoveList.</i>
<i>- Mm?</i>

39
00:01:35,470 --> 00:01:36,679
<i>Wait. Let's take a picture.</i>

40
00:01:37,514 --> 00:01:39,224
<i>I look a mess.</i>
<i>You should've taken it earlier.</i>

41
00:01:39,307 --> 00:01:40,850
<i>Come on, let's take one.</i>

42
00:01:40,934 --> 00:01:41,976
<i>- Okay.</i>
<i>- Give me your phone.</i>

43
00:01:42,060 --> 00:01:44,395
<i>- Why my phone?</i>
<i>- The camera's better.</i>

44
00:01:45,146 --> 00:01:47,524
<i>- Yay! They've made up.</i>
<i>- Cheers!</i>

45
00:01:47,607 --> 00:01:49,067
- [PHONE CHIMES]
- [BILLY] <i>Oh, wait.</i>

46
00:01:49,150 --> 00:01:51,152
<i>- Who is this?</i>
<i>- You're too nosy!</i>

47
00:01:51,861 --> 00:01:54,155
<i>I've already seen it, so just tell me.</i>
<i>Who is it?</i>

48
00:01:55,698 --> 00:01:57,408
<i>Someone I matched with on LoveList.</i>

49
00:01:58,243 --> 00:01:59,869
<i>I thought you were busy.</i>

50
00:01:59,953 --> 00:02:03,331
<i>And weren't you the one who told me</i>
<i>I needed a distraction?</i>

51
00:02:03,414 --> 00:02:04,749
<i>- Yeah.</i>
<i>- Mm-hmm.</i>

52
00:02:04,833 --> 00:02:08,044
<i>If I do find love,</i>

53
00:02:08,128 --> 00:02:10,088
<i>I don't want to call it a distraction.</i>

54
00:02:10,171 --> 00:02:13,675
<i>He should support me more than anyone</i>

55
00:02:13,758 --> 00:02:16,845
<i>so I can stay focused on my goals.</i>

56
00:02:16,928 --> 00:02:18,721
<i>Right? Right?</i>

57
00:02:26,646 --> 00:02:33,653
["ABELYANA" BY MAKI PLAYING]

58
00:02:46,624 --> 00:02:52,046
["ABELYANA" CONTINUES]

59
00:03:07,270 --> 00:03:10,231
["ABELYANA" CONTINUES]

60
00:03:33,838 --> 00:03:37,467
["ABELYANA" CONTINUES]

61
00:03:48,728 --> 00:03:51,022
[SONG ENDS]

62
00:03:53,483 --> 00:03:59,030
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

63
00:04:08,623 --> 00:04:09,624
[FORK CLINKS]

64
00:04:14,712 --> 00:04:17,215
DID YOU LIKE THE CAKE?

65
00:04:17,298 --> 00:04:20,260
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

66
00:04:20,885 --> 00:04:21,970
[PHONE CHIMES]

67
00:04:28,685 --> 00:04:31,437
I ENJOYED IT.

68
00:04:31,521 --> 00:04:37,151
PLEASE THANK BILLY FOR ME.

69
00:04:37,235 --> 00:04:41,406
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

70
00:04:41,489 --> 00:04:42,657
[PHONE CHIMES]

71
00:04:56,421 --> 00:05:01,551
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

72
00:05:02,427 --> 00:05:04,137
THE BILL HAS BEEN PAID, BUT PLEASE,

73
00:05:04,220 --> 00:05:07,682
DON'T MAKE ME
YOUR EMERGENCY CONTACT

74
00:05:07,765 --> 00:05:10,810
BECAUSE NEXT TIME,
I WON'T BE COMING.

75
00:05:16,399 --> 00:05:21,237
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

76
00:05:21,321 --> 00:05:23,573
[PAPER RUSTLING]

77
00:05:28,578 --> 00:05:35,293
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

78
00:06:16,125 --> 00:06:17,085
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

79
00:06:17,168 --> 00:06:19,670
- Billy, hi!
- Morning, Auntie Pres!

80
00:06:19,754 --> 00:06:21,798
- Mmm, perfect timing.
- What's up?

81
00:06:21,881 --> 00:06:22,924
Oh?

82
00:06:23,674 --> 00:06:24,675
[BILLY] Mmm.

83
00:06:25,259 --> 00:06:26,636
For Angels.

84
00:06:27,887 --> 00:06:29,388
Are you sure?

85
00:06:29,472 --> 00:06:30,598
It's all right, Auntie Pres.

86
00:06:30,681 --> 00:06:35,061
LoveList is pretty stable these days,
and it's my promise to you.

87
00:06:35,686 --> 00:06:36,979
Thank you, Billy.

88
00:06:37,063 --> 00:06:40,983
By the way, Sir Eric wanted
to thank you for the cake.

89
00:06:41,067 --> 00:06:42,610
Mmm! Welcome.

90
00:06:42,693 --> 00:06:44,237
- I hope he liked it.
- What?

91
00:06:44,320 --> 00:06:45,404
- [PHONE CHIMES]
- Of course.

92
00:06:45,488 --> 00:06:46,447
Join me for breakfast.

93
00:06:46,531 --> 00:06:47,532
I'm fine.

94
00:06:50,576 --> 00:06:51,953
SORRY, I CAN'T
MAKE IT.

95
00:06:52,036 --> 00:06:53,329
I'M BACK TO
WORK.

96
00:06:53,412 --> 00:06:55,331
AH, OKAY… I GOT USED TO SEEING YOU
AT SCHOOL.

97
00:06:55,414 --> 00:06:58,126
- [PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]
- [CLEARS THROAT]

98
00:06:58,209 --> 00:07:00,002
- What's that, Auntie Pres?
- Huh?

99
00:07:00,086 --> 00:07:01,587
- Care to share?
- [CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

100
00:07:01,671 --> 00:07:03,172
It's nothing. I need to get to work.

101
00:07:03,256 --> 00:07:05,091
- I'm going to be late.
- Oh, she's keeping it a secret.

102
00:07:05,174 --> 00:07:07,552
I left some food in the fridge.

103
00:07:07,635 --> 00:07:09,137
- Just in case you get hungry.
- Okay.

104
00:07:09,220 --> 00:07:10,763
- Okay, bye now.
- Take care, Auntie Pres.

105
00:07:10,847 --> 00:07:11,764
Bye! [GIGGLES]

106
00:07:11,848 --> 00:07:13,766
- Bye!
- Bye-bye!

107
00:07:13,850 --> 00:07:15,435
[FOOTSTEPS RECEDING]

108
00:07:17,270 --> 00:07:22,817
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

109
00:07:25,278 --> 00:07:28,656
[LINE RINGING]

110
00:07:28,739 --> 00:07:30,950
Hi, dude! Good morning!

111
00:07:31,492 --> 00:07:33,786
Auntie Pres's birthday is coming up.

112
00:07:33,870 --> 00:07:35,329
What's our plan?

113
00:07:35,413 --> 00:07:39,709
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

114
00:07:39,792 --> 00:07:42,378
Oh, how about we celebrate at your bar?

115
00:07:45,089 --> 00:07:46,549
Hello? Dude?

116
00:07:48,676 --> 00:07:49,802
Let's see.

117
00:07:50,678 --> 00:07:53,598
Hey, are you okay?

118
00:07:54,140 --> 00:07:55,516
[BREATHES SHARPLY]

119
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:56,851
I'm fine.

120
00:07:57,560 --> 00:07:58,603
I'll get going.

121
00:07:58,686 --> 00:08:00,438
I've got things to do.

122
00:08:00,521 --> 00:08:01,772
Okay.

123
00:08:01,856 --> 00:08:05,359
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

124
00:08:05,443 --> 00:08:06,652
So grumpy.

125
00:08:12,658 --> 00:08:13,910
[SIGHS DEEPLY]

126
00:08:14,952 --> 00:08:17,830
[BIRDS CHIRPING, TRILLING IN DISTANCE]

127
00:08:19,290 --> 00:08:20,958
If we hold it at the bar,

128
00:08:21,042 --> 00:08:23,377
it'll be quite obvious, right?

129
00:08:25,254 --> 00:08:27,965
Maybe we should do it at a resort!

130
00:08:28,049 --> 00:08:29,217
What do you think?

131
00:08:29,300 --> 00:08:30,343
Sounds good.

132
00:08:30,885 --> 00:08:33,179
Oh, a beachside party would be fun too!

133
00:08:33,262 --> 00:08:34,680
Yeah, I suppose.

134
00:08:34,764 --> 00:08:37,725
[KEYBOARD CLACKING]

135
00:08:37,808 --> 00:08:38,809
[LIGHT TAP]

136
00:08:39,310 --> 00:08:40,436
Uh…

137
00:08:40,520 --> 00:08:42,605
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

138
00:08:42,688 --> 00:08:43,814
What?

139
00:08:43,898 --> 00:08:46,567
Are you feeling ill, Jordan?

140
00:08:46,651 --> 00:08:47,944
A little.

141
00:08:48,736 --> 00:08:50,029
- Take the day off.
- No, no--

142
00:08:50,112 --> 00:08:51,656
- Don't work today.
- I can do this.

143
00:08:53,658 --> 00:08:54,825
I can handle myself.

144
00:08:55,618 --> 00:08:56,702
Okay?

145
00:08:56,786 --> 00:08:58,704
- [BREATHES DEEPLY]
- [KEYBOARD CLACKING]

146
00:08:58,788 --> 00:09:03,000
[PHONE RINGING]

147
00:09:03,543 --> 00:09:04,377
Kris?

148
00:09:05,378 --> 00:09:07,213
Hi! [GIGGLES]

149
00:09:07,296 --> 00:09:08,297
Yes?

150
00:09:08,381 --> 00:09:09,423
Oh, you're near?

151
00:09:09,507 --> 00:09:11,217
Okay, I can meet you outside.

152
00:09:12,134 --> 00:09:13,928
Yes. See you in a bit.

153
00:09:14,011 --> 00:09:15,346
See you. Thank you. Thank you.

154
00:09:15,429 --> 00:09:16,597
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

155
00:09:16,681 --> 00:09:17,765
- Check.
- [TAPPING]

156
00:09:17,848 --> 00:09:18,849
- [EXHALES]
- Coffee breath?

157
00:09:18,933 --> 00:09:19,892
[BILLY HUFFING]

158
00:09:19,976 --> 00:09:21,143
Smells like chocolate candy.

159
00:09:22,311 --> 00:09:23,521
- [GRUNTS]
- [GROANS SOFTLY]

160
00:09:23,604 --> 00:09:24,522
You're so grumpy!

161
00:09:24,605 --> 00:09:29,986
[FOOTSTEPS RETREATING]

162
00:09:30,736 --> 00:09:35,825
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

163
00:09:35,908 --> 00:09:39,036
[MUSIC FADING]

164
00:09:41,497 --> 00:09:47,295
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

165
00:09:53,092 --> 00:09:54,552
[VEHICLE APPROACHING]

166
00:10:00,558 --> 00:10:02,560
- Hi, Kris!
- Hi, Billy.

167
00:10:02,643 --> 00:10:04,228
Nice to finally meet you.

168
00:10:04,312 --> 00:10:05,813
Likewise.

169
00:10:05,896 --> 00:10:08,524
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

170
00:10:08,608 --> 00:10:09,567
[MUSIC STOPS]

171
00:10:09,650 --> 00:10:10,776
Jordan.

172
00:10:11,569 --> 00:10:12,820
What are you doing there?

173
00:10:12,903 --> 00:10:14,322
Nothing, uh…

174
00:10:14,405 --> 00:10:15,531
I'm just taking a break.

175
00:10:15,615 --> 00:10:17,283
Okay. Um…

176
00:10:17,366 --> 00:10:20,369
Jordan, I want you to meet
Kristina Salintado.

177
00:10:20,453 --> 00:10:22,163
She's an influencer,

178
00:10:22,246 --> 00:10:25,291
and she wants to do
a special feature for LoveList.

179
00:10:25,374 --> 00:10:27,376
Kris, I want you to meet Jordan,

180
00:10:27,460 --> 00:10:30,254
one of our partners
and tech lead at LoveList.

181
00:10:31,756 --> 00:10:33,591
- Jordan!
- Kris.

182
00:10:34,175 --> 00:10:35,134
You're Kris.

183
00:10:35,217 --> 00:10:36,802
Yes, Kris.

184
00:10:36,886 --> 00:10:38,262
[JORDAN] Okay.

185
00:10:39,055 --> 00:10:41,599
- [KRIS] Yes, nice to meet you.
- I thought…

186
00:10:41,682 --> 00:10:42,558
Never mind.

187
00:10:42,642 --> 00:10:43,809
Thank you so much.

188
00:10:44,518 --> 00:10:46,354
- Wow!
- Yes.

189
00:10:46,437 --> 00:10:48,397
- Kris.
- Kris, yes.

190
00:10:48,481 --> 00:10:49,774
- She's Kris.
- Yeah.

191
00:10:49,857 --> 00:10:52,234
We have a lunch meeting with Kris,

192
00:10:52,318 --> 00:10:54,403
in case you want to join us
if you're not too busy.

193
00:10:54,487 --> 00:10:55,946
- Yes.
- Yes?

194
00:10:56,030 --> 00:10:57,365
- I'll join you.
- Okay.

195
00:10:57,448 --> 00:10:58,824
Let's go, Kris.

196
00:10:58,908 --> 00:11:00,034
- Okay.
- Come in.

197
00:11:05,039 --> 00:11:07,333
[LYDIA] Remember what I told you.

198
00:11:07,416 --> 00:11:09,168
Okay. Thank you.

199
00:11:09,251 --> 00:11:11,420
[WOMAN] Thank you
for sharing your energy with me.

200
00:11:11,504 --> 00:11:12,880
<i>Namaste.</i>

201
00:11:12,963 --> 00:11:16,759
So, why do you look so deep in thought?

202
00:11:16,842 --> 00:11:18,010
[SIGHS]

203
00:11:18,094 --> 00:11:22,515
I don't know if it's right
to feel this way about Sir Eric.

204
00:11:22,598 --> 00:11:25,226
Don't you feel that way about Brandon?

205
00:11:25,309 --> 00:11:26,811
No, this is different.

206
00:11:26,894 --> 00:11:30,314
Then what does Sir Eric have
that Brandon doesn't?

207
00:11:30,398 --> 00:11:35,528
Well, he's understanding, kind,

208
00:11:35,611 --> 00:11:38,781
and especially responsible
when it comes to Oliver.

209
00:11:38,864 --> 00:11:40,116
But Brandon…

210
00:11:40,199 --> 00:11:43,661
You wouldn't know
because you never gave him a chance.

211
00:11:43,744 --> 00:11:45,329
Hey, it's not like that.

212
00:11:45,413 --> 00:11:46,956
It's just that, with Sir Eric,

213
00:11:47,039 --> 00:11:49,375
we've only known each other
for a few weeks,

214
00:11:49,458 --> 00:11:51,502
but I already feel
so comfortable around him.

215
00:11:51,585 --> 00:11:54,213
With Brandon, it's like…

216
00:11:54,296 --> 00:11:55,631
I feel a little awkward.

217
00:11:55,714 --> 00:11:57,174
What's that called?

218
00:11:57,258 --> 00:11:59,343
Wait, is it a rebound or something?

219
00:11:59,427 --> 00:12:00,803
Oh, no, it's not like that.

220
00:12:00,886 --> 00:12:03,389
Besides, I never really had
feelings for Brandon.

221
00:12:03,472 --> 00:12:06,851
I just got my hopes up.
But it wasn't that deep.

222
00:12:07,560 --> 00:12:10,396
I guess LoveList can be wrong too, huh?

223
00:12:10,479 --> 00:12:13,274
It's not LoveList's fault.

224
00:12:13,357 --> 00:12:15,484
I just think you really
have to give it a try

225
00:12:15,568 --> 00:12:17,027
to know for sure.

226
00:12:17,111 --> 00:12:18,195
[GIGGLES]

227
00:12:18,279 --> 00:12:22,074
Then try Sir Eric too.

228
00:12:23,617 --> 00:12:25,411
Just tell him how you feel.

229
00:12:25,494 --> 00:12:28,706
Oh, please. I don't even know
if what I'm feeling for Eric is right.

230
00:12:28,789 --> 00:12:31,250
Are you a teenager? Are you?

231
00:12:31,333 --> 00:12:33,085
Are you still going to play hard to get?

232
00:12:33,169 --> 00:12:35,254
Oh my God. At our age,

233
00:12:35,337 --> 00:12:37,715
we shouldn't waste any more time.

234
00:12:37,798 --> 00:12:39,884
You might end up regretting it.

235
00:12:39,967 --> 00:12:43,220
Didn't you make Rico
court you for ages before too?

236
00:12:43,846 --> 00:12:45,806
Imagine if you'd said yes right away.

237
00:12:45,890 --> 00:12:50,144
You could've been married to Rico
for several years

238
00:12:50,227 --> 00:12:51,770
before he passed away.

239
00:12:52,521 --> 00:12:54,106
Oh gosh, sorry.

240
00:12:54,190 --> 00:12:56,650
- That was a bit much.
- It's okay.

241
00:12:56,734 --> 00:12:58,068
- You're right, though.
- I'm sorry.

242
00:12:58,152 --> 00:12:59,320
It's okay.

243
00:13:01,655 --> 00:13:04,658
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

244
00:13:04,742 --> 00:13:08,787
So, I can do a get-ready-with-me content
for Happily Ever After.

245
00:13:08,871 --> 00:13:10,039
For the bride's side, of course.

246
00:13:10,122 --> 00:13:12,124
But I was thinking,

247
00:13:12,208 --> 00:13:14,502
it'll probably start in the morning

248
00:13:14,585 --> 00:13:16,670
and go through the wedding,
if that's okay?

249
00:13:16,754 --> 00:13:18,422
Yes. That sounds good.

250
00:13:18,506 --> 00:13:20,007
But also, if I may suggest,

251
00:13:20,090 --> 00:13:22,718
I think people like seeing
what's happening beforehand,

252
00:13:22,801 --> 00:13:24,720
so maybe we could do
a split-screen treatment?

253
00:13:24,803 --> 00:13:27,306
Like his-and-hers POVs.
What do you think?

254
00:13:27,389 --> 00:13:28,974
I see where you're going.
Yeah, I love that.

255
00:13:29,058 --> 00:13:30,309
- Yes?
- Yeah, let's do it.

256
00:13:30,392 --> 00:13:31,852
Let's just capture the candid moments

257
00:13:31,936 --> 00:13:35,105
because people like seeing
the natural side of the bride and groom.

258
00:13:35,189 --> 00:13:39,485
Yeah, just let me know if we need more
cameras or POVs of other shots.

259
00:13:39,568 --> 00:13:41,737
No, I think
what you proposed earlier is enough,

260
00:13:41,820 --> 00:13:43,030
since you have a limited…

261
00:13:43,113 --> 00:13:45,324
What do you think? Any suggestions?

262
00:13:45,407 --> 00:13:46,909
- [KRIS] Yeah.
- Um…

263
00:13:47,868 --> 00:13:49,245
Yep, it's good.

264
00:13:49,328 --> 00:13:51,580
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

265
00:13:51,664 --> 00:13:54,333
- [AWKWARD GIGGLE]
- You mean the content?

266
00:13:54,416 --> 00:13:56,460
- Oh, the content?
- [BILLY] Mm-hmm.

267
00:13:56,544 --> 00:13:57,920
[KRIS] Yeah.

268
00:13:58,003 --> 00:13:59,255
Billy knows best.

269
00:14:00,673 --> 00:14:02,424
For the content. Yeah.

270
00:14:02,508 --> 00:14:04,718
Okay, I think we're all set.

271
00:14:04,802 --> 00:14:05,970
- Okay.
- Yes.

272
00:14:06,053 --> 00:14:08,681
Thank you so much. Go eat first.

273
00:14:08,764 --> 00:14:13,269
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

274
00:14:13,352 --> 00:14:15,312
[MUSIC FADES]

275
00:14:18,440 --> 00:14:25,364
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

276
00:14:35,916 --> 00:14:36,834
[ENRICO] <i>Olive.</i>

277
00:14:38,168 --> 00:14:41,463
<i>Do I really have to stay away</i>
<i>from our children now?</i>

278
00:14:42,715 --> 00:14:44,884
<i>I want to apologize to Billy,</i>

279
00:14:45,593 --> 00:14:48,178
<i>but I don't want to make things</i>
<i>harder for her.</i>

280
00:14:48,804 --> 00:14:50,556
<i>What should I do?</i>

281
00:14:50,639 --> 00:14:54,351
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

282
00:14:55,477 --> 00:14:56,520
Once this is sorted out,

283
00:14:56,604 --> 00:14:59,023
have the team on standby
for our next meeting.

284
00:14:59,106 --> 00:15:00,190
Thank you.

285
00:15:01,400 --> 00:15:02,484
[JORDAN] Dude.

286
00:15:02,568 --> 00:15:04,194
You know what Auntie Pres would like?

287
00:15:04,278 --> 00:15:06,071
- Hmm?
- Filipino food.

288
00:15:06,155 --> 00:15:08,616
- That's her favorite.
- Correct.

289
00:15:08,699 --> 00:15:09,992
It should be a Filipino restaurant.

290
00:15:10,075 --> 00:15:12,286
I know the perfect place.
I'll take care of it.

291
00:15:12,369 --> 00:15:14,455
- Mm-hmm.
- And there should be games too.

292
00:15:14,538 --> 00:15:15,539
Mm, okay.

293
00:15:15,623 --> 00:15:19,126
Those Filipino street games we used to
play when we were kids. Remember?

294
00:15:19,209 --> 00:15:21,211
Auntie Pres is going to love it, I know.

295
00:15:21,295 --> 00:15:22,463
- Really?
- Yeah.

296
00:15:22,546 --> 00:15:23,756
- Are you sure?
- Yeah.

297
00:15:23,839 --> 00:15:25,716
Let me see. Oh, you're not sick anymore.

298
00:15:25,799 --> 00:15:27,885
You're so happy and full of energy now.

299
00:15:27,968 --> 00:15:30,054
- Huh?
- Good mood today, huh?

300
00:15:30,137 --> 00:15:31,347
I wonder why.

301
00:15:32,014 --> 00:15:33,349
You like her, don't you?

302
00:15:36,268 --> 00:15:37,186
Kris?

303
00:15:38,187 --> 00:15:39,021
- Mmm.
- No.

304
00:15:39,104 --> 00:15:40,689
Then why did you go downstairs earlier?

305
00:15:40,773 --> 00:15:43,442
You even went to greet her.
And you keep repeating her name.

306
00:15:43,525 --> 00:15:45,611
- Mm? Mm? Mm?
- Dude! It's not like that.

307
00:15:45,694 --> 00:15:46,946
- You got it all wrong.
- Oh, really?

308
00:15:47,029 --> 00:15:47,863
- Me?
- Yeah.

309
00:15:47,947 --> 00:15:50,199
You're so happy now.

310
00:15:50,282 --> 00:15:51,867
You're having a lot of fun now.

311
00:15:51,951 --> 00:15:53,702
- Fine, you don't like her.
- I thought…

312
00:15:53,786 --> 00:15:55,579
You don't like her because you like me.

313
00:15:55,663 --> 00:15:57,247
- Huh?
- Me.

314
00:15:58,248 --> 00:15:59,416
Whatever.

315
00:15:59,500 --> 00:16:00,584
You don't like that?

316
00:16:01,835 --> 00:16:03,379
You're too gullible.

317
00:16:03,462 --> 00:16:04,880
Come on. Back to work.

318
00:16:12,179 --> 00:16:13,597
<i>Federico,</i>

319
00:16:13,681 --> 00:16:15,182
<i>you'll always be in my heart.</i>

320
00:16:15,265 --> 00:16:16,642
<i>You know that.</i>

321
00:16:16,725 --> 00:16:19,895
<i>But now, someone else is</i>
<i>making me happy again,</i>

322
00:16:19,979 --> 00:16:22,815
<i>just like you used to.</i>

323
00:16:23,357 --> 00:16:24,483
<i>But I don't know.</i>

324
00:16:24,566 --> 00:16:26,110
<i>I feel guilty.</i>

325
00:16:26,193 --> 00:16:29,613
<i>I don't know if you're happy for me.</i>

326
00:16:30,364 --> 00:16:33,659
<i>No matter what happens,</i>
<i>I'll never forget you.</i>

327
00:16:33,742 --> 00:16:35,077
<i>I love you, Federico.</i>

328
00:16:35,160 --> 00:16:38,288
<i>Even though I think</i>
<i>I'm falling in love again.</i>

329
00:16:38,372 --> 00:16:42,209
<i>Please give me a sign</i>
<i>if it's right to feel this way.</i>

330
00:16:44,920 --> 00:16:51,885
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

331
00:17:09,695 --> 00:17:15,617
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

332
00:17:26,378 --> 00:17:27,421
Sir Eric.

333
00:17:27,504 --> 00:17:34,053
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

334
00:17:34,136 --> 00:17:36,805
You can tell me anything.

335
00:17:36,889 --> 00:17:38,474
Is it about your family?

336
00:17:39,224 --> 00:17:42,561
Does it have something to do with
your emergency the other day?

337
00:17:44,938 --> 00:17:45,939
[PRECIOUS EXHALES]

338
00:17:46,023 --> 00:17:48,150
If you're not ready to talk, that's fine.

339
00:17:48,233 --> 00:17:50,319
Just know that I'm here for you, Sir Eric.

340
00:17:52,738 --> 00:17:53,864
Just call me Eric.

341
00:17:53,947 --> 00:17:55,032
Mm.

342
00:17:55,115 --> 00:17:58,368
Okay. I'm here for you, Eric.

343
00:17:58,452 --> 00:18:03,373
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

344
00:18:03,457 --> 00:18:05,584
Thanks for

345
00:18:05,667 --> 00:18:07,586
keeping me company.

346
00:18:07,669 --> 00:18:09,338
Don't mention it.

347
00:18:09,421 --> 00:18:12,132
You have done so much for Oliver.

348
00:18:12,216 --> 00:18:15,719
You treat him like family.

349
00:18:16,637 --> 00:18:19,431
I just want to repay your kindness.

350
00:18:21,767 --> 00:18:27,106
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

351
00:18:44,456 --> 00:18:50,003
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

352
00:19:02,182 --> 00:19:03,809
Wow!

353
00:19:03,892 --> 00:19:06,228
You're up early, Ms. Supervisor.

354
00:19:06,311 --> 00:19:07,521
Are you leaving already?

355
00:19:07,604 --> 00:19:09,648
Well, I have to.

356
00:19:09,731 --> 00:19:14,027
I have a lot of work to do as supervisor.

357
00:19:14,111 --> 00:19:14,945
Ah…

358
00:19:15,028 --> 00:19:17,322
Well, if your sister were here,

359
00:19:17,406 --> 00:19:19,491
she'd be proud of you.

360
00:19:19,575 --> 00:19:21,952
You're successful, just like her.

361
00:19:22,035 --> 00:19:23,996
Hmm? Do your best, dear.

362
00:19:24,079 --> 00:19:26,623
I will, like I always do.

363
00:19:26,707 --> 00:19:28,208
All right, take care!

364
00:19:30,210 --> 00:19:36,258
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

365
00:19:51,857 --> 00:19:54,651
[ENRICO] <i>They see her</i>
<i>as their real mother.</i>

366
00:19:54,735 --> 00:19:56,403
<i>All the more reason</i>
<i>why you should come clean.</i>

367
00:19:56,486 --> 00:19:58,530
<i>It'll help lighten the burden</i>
<i>you're carrying.</i>

368
00:19:58,614 --> 00:19:59,990
<i>Can we meet?</i>

369
00:20:00,073 --> 00:20:01,742
<i>I'm done second-guessing!</i>

370
00:20:01,825 --> 00:20:03,285
<i>I'm taking the risk!</i>

371
00:20:03,368 --> 00:20:05,370
<i>There's something</i>
<i>I need to confess.</i>

372
00:20:05,454 --> 00:20:08,582
<i>I didn't expect Auntie Pres</i>
<i>to find love again.</i>

373
00:20:08,665 --> 00:20:11,210
<i>Now, she has</i>
<i>more reasons to smile.</i>

374
00:20:12,377 --> 00:20:15,380
<i>- ♪ Why is it like that? ♪</i>
- [FANS CHEER]

375
00:20:16,465 --> 00:20:22,679
<i>♪ So many are rushing</i>
<i>To get ahead ♪</i>

376
00:20:22,763 --> 00:20:23,847
<i>♪ Yeah ♪</i>

377
00:20:23,931 --> 00:20:25,766
<i>Why does he treat us this way?</i>

378
00:20:25,849 --> 00:20:28,143
<i>Happy birthday to me.</i>

379
00:20:28,227 --> 00:20:30,229
<i>Can I take you out to dinner later?</i>

380
00:20:30,312 --> 00:20:33,732
<i>Do you know</i>
<i>who Auntie Pres is dating?</i>

381
00:20:33,815 --> 00:20:35,442
<i>Hasn't she told you?</i>

382
00:20:35,525 --> 00:20:38,570
<i>It's Sir Eric.</i>
<i>Your aunt is dating Sir Eric.</i>

383
00:20:38,654 --> 00:20:40,906
<i>- Surprise!</i>
<i>- Surprise!</i>

384
00:20:40,989 --> 00:20:43,325
[CHEERING]

385
00:20:43,408 --> 00:20:44,576
[PRECIOUS] <i>Billy!</i>

386
00:20:48,997 --> 00:20:51,375
<i>You just won't leave us alone.</i>

387
00:20:51,959 --> 00:20:53,669
<i>I only asked for one thing.</i>

388
00:20:53,752 --> 00:20:55,671
<i>- Billy--</i>
- [BILLY] <i>Just leave.</i>

389
00:20:55,754 --> 00:20:57,506
<i>Billy, what's going on?</i>

390
00:20:57,589 --> 00:20:59,549
<i>How could you be so selfish?</i>

391
00:20:59,633 --> 00:21:02,886
<i>You even made a fool of the person</i>
<i>who raised us and cared for us</i>

392
00:21:02,970 --> 00:21:05,013
<i>when that should have been you?!</i>
